{"n": 767, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "767.webp", "text": "30 41725\n\n30 41726\n\n30.41 727\n\n=\n\n30 at t78\n\n41-014.\n\nREPAIRING GLASS FIBER\nREINFORCED PLASTIC PARTS\n\nAssumed Damage:\n\nHole or Damaged Laminate in Outer Trunk\nLid Panel Between Reinforcement Ribs:\nNote:\n\nThe following repaizing instructions can only\ndescribe general procedures.\n\nProcedures must be adapted to the pertinent\ntype of damage.\n\nSee introduction for additional information.\n\nCut out damaged area until firm, non-fibrous\nlaminate is visiblo,\n\nNote:\n\nGrind off that much further, if gasoline, oll\nor something similar has penetrated into the\ndamaged area.\n\nNote:\n\nThe trunk lid consists of inside and outside\npanels.\n\nIf both panels are damaged, cut out the\ndamaged area on the inside a little larger.\n\nGrind mating surfaces in {lat-flowing transition.\nNote:\n\nThe plastic surface has a graphite coat to make\nin conductive for the painting method used in\nstandard production.\n\nGrind off the graphite coat outside of the\ndamaged area.\n\nClean ambient ares with stoetone.\n\n2041729\n\n3041732\n\n(Coat mating surfaces with an adhesion agent,\n\nRemove repair damage from aluminum foil\nand cut off to size.\n\nimportant!\n\nMaterial hardens in sunshine,\n\nClose aluminum bag immediately to keep out\nlight.\n\nPull off transparent plastic sheet on one side.\n\nPlace repair bandage on the damaged surface\nand press on all around.\n\nPress out air bubbles.\n\nUse a rubber roller, if necessary.", "words": [["30", 0.2012, 0.2646, 0.2123, 0.2804], ["41725", 0.2164, 0.2698, 0.2467, 0.2778], ["30", 0.2022, 0.504, 0.2133, 0.5132], ["41726", 0.2164, 0.5053, 0.2457, 0.5132], ["30.41", 0.2042, 0.7374, 0.2255, 0.7467], ["727", 0.2305, 0.7374, 0.2457, 0.7454], ["=", 0.2305, 0.7784, 0.2503, 0.7903], ["30", 0.2002, 0.9749, 0.2103, 0.9828], ["at", 0.2154, 0.9749, 0.2235, 0.9815], ["t78", 0.2295, 0.9749, 0.2437, 0.9828], ["41-014.", 0.4671, 0.0258, 0.544, 0.0496], ["REPAIRING", 0.